---
title: Olive oil cake
servings: 10
tags: [baking, dessert]
source: Invented for this repository
---

Heat the oven to 175°C and line a #23cm cake tin{}.

Whisk the @eggs{3} with the @caster sugar{200%g} in a #large bowl{} until pale
and thick, ~{4%minutes}.

Pour in the @olive oil{180%ml} in a thin stream, whisking, then the
@whole milk{120%ml}.

Fold in the @plain flour{240%g}, @baking powder{2%tsp} and @fine salt{1/2%tsp}
in two additions, stopping as soon as the flour disappears.

Bake ~{45%minutes} until a skewer comes out clean. Cool in the tin ~{20%minutes}
before turning out.
